        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "40045564-69f7-5932-986a-94be241d9815",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Petruccio Ubaldini, Elizabeth I of England, Henry VIII, Edward VI, Horace Walpole\n- Organizations: Bodleian Library, British Museum, King's Library, House of Tudor\n- Roles: mercenary soldier, calligraphist, illuminator, queen, monarch\n\nFacts:\n- Elizabeth I of England was born on 7 September 1533.\n- Petruccio Ubaldini, a Tuscan Italian born around 1524 and died around 1600, served as a mercenary soldier for Henry VIII from 1545 to 1547.\n- Petruccio Ubaldini served in Edward VI's Scottish war in 1549.\n- Elizabeth I of England became Queen of England and Ireland on 17 November 1558.\n- Petruccio Ubaldini worked in England during the reign of Elizabeth I and appears to have enjoyed favor at her court.\n- Petruccio Ubaldini was also a calligraphist and illuminator on vellum.\n- Petruccio Ubaldini presented an illuminated book to Elizabeth I, and that book is in the Bodleian Library.\n- Horace Walpole listed other works by Petruccio Ubaldini that had formerly been in the King's Library and are now mostly in the British Museum.\n- Elizabeth I of England was sometimes called The Virgin Queen, Gloriana, and Good Queen Bess.\n- Elizabeth I of England was the last monarch of the House of Tudor and reigned until her death on 24 March 1603.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "347bb199-81db-5ae5-a8d2-298532750b80",
        "text": "Page: Petruccio Ubaldini. Sentence: Petruccio Ubaldini (ca.1524–ca.1600) was an Italian (\"Tuscan\") mercenary soldier for Henry VIII (1545–47) and in Edward VI's Scottish war (1549) a calligraphist and illuminator on vellum, who was working in England in the reign of Queen Elizabeth, and seems to have enjoyed the favor of the Court.\nPage: Petruccio Ubaldini. Sentence: One of his illuminated books, presented by him to Elizabeth, is in the Bodleian Library, and Walpole gives a list of other works, formerly in the King's Library, and now, most of them, in the British Museum.\nPage: Elizabeth I of England. Sentence: Elizabeth I (7 September 1533 – 24 March 1603) was Queen of England and Ireland from 17 November 1558 until her death.\nPage: Elizabeth I of England. Sentence: Sometimes called The Virgin Queen, Gloriana or Good Queen Bess, Elizabeth was the last monarch of the House of Tudor.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
